\par\par \uc2 MAUREEN DOWD\par \uc2 Editorial Desk; SECTSR\par \b \uc2 Republicans' Unholy Alliances\b0\par\par\uc2 By Maureen Dowd \par \uc2 895 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 October 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON -- This will sound quaint.\par \par \uc2 In May 2016, The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  ran the story of how Donald Trump, in his real estate days, would call reporters, pretending to be his own spokesman, to brag and leak nuggets about nonexistent romances with famous women. I thought that would knock him out of the race.\par \par \uc2 The story hit on a Friday, so I scrambled to rewrite my column on the assumption that Trump wouldn't last the weekend.\par \par \uc2 But the scoop didn't make a dent.\par \par \uc2 The next day, The Times splashed a piece on the front page reporting that dozens of women had accused Trump of ''unwelcome romantic advances'' and lewd and ''unending commentary on the female form.''\par \par \uc2 Again, he emerged unscathed with his base.\par \par \uc2 I still didn't learn my lesson, though. That October, when the ''Access Hollywood'' tape showed Trump yucking it up about kissing, groping and trying to have sex with women, noting that ''when you're a star, they let you do it,'' I once more figured he couldn't survive as leader of the party of ''family values'' and the religious right.\par \par \uc2 He could.\par \par \uc2 Once, there were limits, things that could disqualify you from office, especially in the party that claimed a special relationship with Jesus.\par \par \uc2 But those limits don't exist anymore.\par \par \uc2 Conservatives have sacrificed any claim to principle. In an unholy transaction, they stuck with Trump because there was a Supreme Court seat and they were willing to tolerate his moral void in order to hijack the court. They didn't care how he treated women as long as he gave them the opportunity to rip away rights from women. They wanted to impose their warped morality, a ''Handmaid's Tale'' world, on the rest of us.\par \par \uc2 Christian-right leaders made clear that, no matter what Trump said or did to women, he was preferable to \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , who supported \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Jerry Falwell Jr\uc2 . said at the time, ''We're never going to have a perfect candidate unless Jesus Christ is on the ballot,'' noting, ''We're all sinners.''\par \par \uc2 Well, Falwell certainly was. Four years later, he was ousted from running \uc2 Liberty University\uc2  after a sex scandal of his own.\par \par \uc2 Now, in Georgia, conservatives are turning a blind eye to sordid stories coming out about \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , who demonstrates no qualifications for serving in the Senate. His sole credential is that he was once excellent at carrying a football.\par \par \uc2 Story after story has emerged about reprehensible behavior and lies concerning women and children, and about falsifying his personal history.\par \par \uc2 The Daily Beast asserted that while Walker wants to completely ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even in cases of rape, incest and the life of the mother, comparing it to murder, he paid for a girlfriend's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2009. Walker has called the story ''a flat-out lie,'' but The Beast talked to the unnamed woman and checked her financial records. She said she was just sick of the hypocrisy. Even his conservative influencer son, Christian, disparaged his father's ''lies'' on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Friday, The Times published a story confirming The Daily Beast's reporting, and in a startling development added that in 2011, Herschel pressured the same woman to have another \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They ended their relationship when she refused; she had their son, now 10.\par \par \uc2 There's more: His ex-wife claimed he pointed a pistol at her head and told her he was going to blow her brains out; he has four children with four different women, but hadn't publicly acknowledged three of them. His 10-year-old was one of those hidden.\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  and his fellow Republicans should be ashamed to promote this troubled person for their own benefit.\par \par \uc2 Privately, some Republicans are mortified by the Walker spiral, but they're going to brazen it out for the win.\par \par \uc2 Dana Loesch\uc2 , the right-wing radio host, was blunt: ''I don't care if \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  paid to abort endangered baby eagles. I want control of the Senate.''\par \par \uc2 Republicans have exposed their willingness to accept anything to get power that they then abuse. As \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  said out loud, with his fellow Republicans shushing him, they want a nationwide ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks. And \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  is key to that.\par \par \uc2 Trump got to know Walker when he bought the New Jersey Generals in 1983, which Walker had joined after he won the Heisman Trophy and dropped out of the University of Georgia to turn pro.\par \par \uc2 ''In a lot of ways, Mr. Trump became a mentor to me,'' Walker wrote in his memoir in 2008, ''and I modeled myself and my business practices after him.'' Trump led the cry ''Run, Herschel, run!''\par \par \uc2 Walker takes after his mentor with his lies, hypocrisy and know-nothingness on issues. Still worse, he's following his mentor by denying his transgressions as a womanizer, even as he tries to smash women's rights.\par \par \uc2 The Times is committed to publishing a diversity of letters to the editor. We'd like to hear what you think about this or any of our articles. Here are some tips . And here's our email: letters@nytimes.com .\par \par \uc2 Follow The \uc2 New York Times\uc2  Opinion section on \uc2 Facebook\uc2  , \uc2 Twitter\uc2  (@NYTopinion) and \uc2 Instagram\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 (PHOTOGRAPH BY Ben Gray/Associated Press FOR THE NEW YORK TIMES) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020221009eia90004w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
