\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Biden Urges Voter Action As White House Steps In To Protect  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Access\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alan Rappeport \par \uc2 795 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 October 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 15\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 President Biden urged voters to make their voices heard to preserve \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON -- President Biden unveiled new measures on Tuesday to protect access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , 100 days after the Supreme Court ended the constitutional right to terminate a pregnancy, and called on Americans to pressure Congress to pass legislation that would ensure \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal across the United States.\par \par \uc2 The actions came as \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  have become a central issue in political campaigns across the nation ahead of next month's midterm elections. Democrats have seized on the court's decision to overturn Roe v. Wade to motivate voters to elect lawmakers who will expand \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationally and block Republicans from imposing further restrictions.\par \par \uc2 ''Right now we're short a handful of votes,'' Mr. Biden said as he convened his task force on \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the White House. ''The only way it's going to happen is if the American people make it happen.''\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden assailed Republican lawmakers who have been pushing for a national ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and urged voters to remember what was at stake if Democrats lost control of power in Washington.\par \par \uc2 ''It means that even if you live in a state where extremist Republican officials aren't running the show, your right to choose will still be at risk,'' Mr. Biden said.\par \par \uc2 Most abortions are now banned in at least 14 states, and others are engaged in legal fights over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. Biden administration officials estimate that nearly 30 million women of reproductive age now live in a state with a ban and that about 22 million women cannot access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care after six weeks.\par \par \uc2 The White House said Tuesday that the Department of Education will issue a reminder to universities that they cannot discriminate against students on the basis of pregnancy, including if a pregnancy has been terminated.\par \par \uc2 Additionally, the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  is announcing $6 million in grants to expand access to family planning clinics that receive Title X federal funding. The White House has asked Congress for an additional $400 million for the clinics.\par \par \uc2 The White House believes that public sentiment is on its side when it comes to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Pew Research Center\uc2  survey this summer showed that 61 percent of Americans believe that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in most cases, though the political divide over those questions has become more stark.\par \par \uc2 In close races around the country, Democrats are amplifying the issue. The House Democrats' super PAC is investing heavily in advertisements focused on \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including one that dramatizes the consequences of a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. It features police officers handcuffing doctors, nurses and patients who sought or performed ''health care services that have been legal for nearly 50 years.''\par \par \uc2 Some Republicans have tried to play down \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in favor of a focus on crime and inflation. However, the issue re-emerged last month when Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , Republican of South Carolina, introduced legislation that would institute a federal ban on abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy. Senator \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the minority leader, has said that he does not expect Republicans to try to enact a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has faced criticism for failing to do more to protect the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights of women after the court's decision this year. Despite calls from some activists to declare a public health emergency to expand \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, White House officials have been skeptical about what such a move would achieve and leery of inviting new legal fights.\par \par \uc2 In a memo ahead of the announcement, Jennifer Klein, director of the White House's Gender Policy Council, laid out some of the steps that the Biden administration has taken to preserve \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. She pointed to executive orders defending the right to travel across state lines for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and guidance intended to ensure that doctors can provide abortions in cases in which patients are ''presenting with an emergency medical condition'' and need to be stabilized.\par \par \uc2 But White House officials acknowledged that there was only so much that they could do to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access without Congress and cast \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a moral matter.\par \par \uc2 ''I certainly believe that a woman should have the freedom to make decisions about her own body and that her government should not be making those decisions for her,'' Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said at the task force meeting. ''Today extremist so-called leaders are attacking the freedom and liberty of millions of women at a state level.''\par \par \uc2 President Biden on Tuesday assailed lawmakers pushing for a national \uc2  ban after the Supreme Court ruling. (PHOTOGRAPH BY PETE MAROVICH FOR THE NEW YORK TIMES) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020221005eia50003t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
