\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Report Says Walker Paid For  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  For Girlfriend\b0\par\par\uc2 By Maya King \par \uc2 766 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 October 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 19\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Mr. Walker called the report a lie, after The Daily Beast, which has also broken news about Mr. Walker's out-of-wedlock children, reported that a former girlfriend had the procedure in 2009.\par \par \uc2 ATLANTA -- \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , the Republican nominee for \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  in Georgia and an avowed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponent, paid for his then-girlfriend to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2009, according to a report published Monday in The Daily Beast. Mr. Walker called the claim ''a flat-out lie.''\par \par \uc2 The woman, who The Daily Beast said asked to remain anonymous out of privacy concerns, said that she and Mr. Walker had conceived the child while the two were dating, and mutually agreed not to go ahead with the pregnancy. She said Mr. Walker, who was not married at the time, reimbursed her for the cost of the procedure, the outlet reported.\par \par \uc2 As evidence, the woman provided a copy of a $700 check from Mr. Walker, a receipt from the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic and a ''get well'' card from Mr. Walker, The Daily Beast reported. The outlet published a photo of the card with what it said was Mr. Walker's signature.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Walker quickly posted a statement on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  and threatened to file a defamation lawsuit against The Daily Beast on Tuesday morning. ''I deny this in the strongest possible terms,'' he said. ''It's disgusting, gutter politics.''\par \par \uc2 The development is the latest in a series of potentially damaging reports about Mr. Walker's personal life since he began his campaign for Senate in 2021. In June, The Daily Beast reported that Mr. Walker, who has criticized absentee fathers in Black households, had fathered a child out of wedlock. Later that week, the outlet reported on two more children he had not previously mentioned publicly or to his campaign aides.\par \par \uc2 Christian Walker, Mr. Walker's son who has not endorsed his father's campaign or appeared publicly on behalf of his father, weighed in on Monday evening, saying on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  that ''every member'' of Mr. Walker's family urged him not to run for office.\par \par \uc2 ''I don't care about someone who has a bad past and takes accountability. But how DARE YOU LIE and act as though you're some 'moral, Christian, upright man,''' he continued. ''You've lived a life of DESTROYING other peoples lives.''\par \par \uc2 Mr. Walker responded with a single tweet: ''I LOVE my son no matter what.''\par \par \uc2 In an interview on Monday night with \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2  of Fox News, Mr. Walker denied the account laid out in The Daily Beast article, saying he did not know the woman. When asked about the reported $700 payment for the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said, ''I send money to a lot of people.''\par \par \uc2 ''I never asked anyone to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I never paid for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,'' Mr. Walker continued. He said of Democrats, ''They want this seat. But right now they've energized me even more.''\par \par \uc2 Mr. Walker has also been found to have exaggerated or misrepresented other parts of his life story. He claimed to have worked in law enforcement when he did not. He exaggerated the origins of a chicken business he built. After starting a food distribution company, he claimed to donate a portion of his business earnings to charity but there is little proof that the organizations received the funds.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Walker has made his opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a cornerstone of his campaign message, saying repeatedly that he supports bans on the procedure with no exceptions for rape or incest. He has also endorsed legislation recently proposed by Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , a Republican from South Carolina, that institutes a national ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks of pregnancy. Mr. Graham's bill does include exceptions for rape, incest or pregnancies that threaten the mother's health.\par \par \uc2 ''There's no exceptions in my mind,'' Mr. Walker told reporters in Macon, Ga., in May, days before the state's G.O.P. Senate primary. ''You never know what a child is going to become.''\par \par \uc2 The Georgia Senate race is one of the most closely watched in the country. Most polls show that the race between Mr. Walker and his Democratic opponent, Senator Raphael Warnock, is virtually tied. A spokeswoman for Mr. Warnock's campaign declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 Herschel Walker campaigning in July in Georgia. He has faced a number of damaging reports about his life story since he began his campaign for Senate in 2021. (PHOTOGRAPH BY Nicole Craine for The New York Times FOR THE NEW YORK TIMES) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020221004eia40004c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
