\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 In Tight Arizona Governor's Race, a Democrat Runs on  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Rights\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jack Healy and Jazmine Ulloa \par \uc2 1,776 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 September 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 21\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  has struggled to compete against Republican Kari Lake, who is running on border security and election fraud conspiracy theories.\par \par \uc2 PHOENIX -- Here was a debate that \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  wanted to have.\par \par \uc2 For weeks, critics heckled Ms. Hobbs as a ''coward'' and ''chicken'' for refusing to share a debate stage with her combative, election-denying Republican rival in the race to become Arizona's next governor. Some fellow Democrats fretted it was a dodge that risked alienating undecided voters who could tip the race's razor-thin margin.\par \par \uc2 Then last Friday, a judge upended the campaign by resurrecting an 1864 law that bans nearly all abortions across Arizona, a ruling made possible by the overturning of Roe v. Wade. And Ms. Hobbs, Arizona's Democratic secretary of state, seized what Democrats in this battleground state hoped would become a galvanizing moment.\par \par \uc2 She scrapped a campaign event and scrambled to arrange a news conference outside the office of the Republican state attorney general who had argued to reimpose the Old West-era \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law. She vowed to repeal the ban and taunted Republicans for their muted responses to the abrupt halt of all abortions across Arizona.\par \par \uc2 She also spoke in starkly personal terms about how she had once had a miscarriage, and had needed a surgical procedure now being denied to women in states that have outlawed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Ms. Hobbs says any \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  decisions should ''rest solely between a woman and her doctor, not the government.''\par \par \uc2 ''It's difficult,'' Ms. Hobbs said later about sharing her own story. ''But there's too much at stake in this election not to talk about that.''\par \par \uc2 The race for an open governor's seat in Arizona has swelled into a bruising struggle over the evolving political identity of a traditionally conservative state that sends Democrats to Washington, while keeping Republicans in power at home.\par \par \uc2 The question now is whether Arizona will move left with Ms. Hobbs, a soft-spoken social worker and state politician, or veer deeper into MAGA territory by electing Kari Lake, a former local news anchor running on militarizing the nation's southwestern border and amplifying falsehoods about the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 ''I really think this is a battle between two competing narratives,'' said Kirk Adams, a Republican former speaker of the Arizona House and former chief of staff for the outgoing Republican governor, \uc2 Doug Ducey\uc2 . ''\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and saving democracy on one hand and inflation and border security and a stolen election on the other.''\par \par \uc2 As secretary of state during the 2020 presidential election, Ms. Hobbs became a hero to Democrats for defending Arizona's voting system from an onslaught of false accusations of fraud. She vaulted to the front of the Democratic primary for governor while also becoming a target of death threats and protests.\par \par \uc2 Her supporters cast the race against Ms. Lake as ''sanity versus chaos,'' and said Ms. Hobbs would take a bipartisan approach to tackling Arizona's water shortages, meager school funding and spiraling housing costs. But even some supporters doubt whether her mild manner can stand up to Lake's bolder one.\par \par \uc2 ''I don't think she has done as well as she should have,'' said Claudia Underwood, a retired lawyer and Democrat in a corner of Phoenix with enviable views of Camelback Mountain, the city's most famous peak. ''She is not coming across as strong as I think she should.''\par \par \uc2 Ms. Lake has spent the race lobbing verbal grenades at Ms. Hobbs with a delivery honed during years anchoring local Fox newscasts. She has called for Ms. Hobbs to be jailed and needles her as ''Katie.'' Ms. Hobbs uses Ms. Lake's full name or formally calls her ''my opponent.''\par \par \uc2 While Ms. Lake has given speeches in front of roaring crowds at Trump rallies, Ms. Hobbs has run a campaign centered on smaller events with local and tribal leaders and student organizers, and house parties with supporters.\par \par \uc2 Supporters say she is genuine and caring, but even on the most comfortable terrain, she sometimes sticks to the script. At a recent roundtable with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters, she hewed largely to prepared statements.\par \par \uc2 ''She's not going to get up at a rally like Ms. Lake does and get the crowd all stirred up,'' said State Senator Lela Alston, a Democrat who once ran with Ms. Hobbs and U.S. Senator \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  for their state legislative seats. ''She's much more thoughtful and available to people all over the state. I'm hoping the message gets out.''\par \par \uc2 A handful of Democrats running for state legislative races said they had yet to get an invitation to campaign with her or appear together at an event. By contrast, Ms. Lake had two Republican state legislative candidates introduce themselves before she appeared at a friendly question-and-answer session with supporters.\par \par \uc2 ''We have a candidate who isn't out campaigning, so it's hard to break through and keep those issues relevant if there's nobody out there talking about them,'' said Marco Lopez, Ms. Hobbs's Democratic primary opponent.\par \par \uc2 Billy Grant, a consultant for Ms. Lake, has said that her campaign has focused on showing the clear contrasts between the two candidates and that she considered the border to be the top issue for voters in Arizona.\par \par \uc2 ''\uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  was convinced she could win with the \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  strategy of just running TV ads and hiding out from the public,'' he said. ''That is just not going to happen.''\par \par \uc2 Other Democrats argued Ms. Hobbs was right in running her own campaign and declining to debate an opponent who wrongly insists the 2020 election was stolen. The Republican nominees for Arizona's most powerful statewide office this November have all made repeated false claims that the 2020 vote was fraudulent and rightfully won by Mr. Trump.\par \par \uc2 Racism and discrimination have also come up in uncomfortable ways for Ms. Hobbs. In November, a jury awarded $2.75 million to a Black staff member who worked under Ms. Hobbs in the State Senate, and who was fired in 2015 after complaining about her unequal pay.\par \par \uc2 The former staffer, Talonya Adams, has become a vocal critic of Ms. Hobbs, and Ms. Lake has used the lawsuit to call Ms. Hobbs a ''convicted racist.'' Ms. Hobbs released a statement apologizing to Ms. Adams.\par \par \uc2 Now, about two weeks before ballots are mailed out, interviews with voters across Arizona suggest that people's priorities are splintered. While many Democrats cite \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and democracy as top concerns, others who are just now tuning into the race say they are most worried about soaring food and rent costs and an increase in migrants attempting to cross Arizona's southern border.\par \par \uc2 Jon Hernandez, 22, who says he is undecided but leaning toward voting for Ms. Lake, has spent the summer living at home with his parents and doing the ''soul draining'' work of a failed job hunt. He said he supported the Clinton-era pitch that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal, safe and rare. But he said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a lesser concern.\par \par \uc2 ''It's nowhere near as important,'' he said. ''If we don't get control of rampant inflation and gas prices, that spells disaster for much more of the population. It's like tiers of priorities.''\par \par \uc2 In an interview, Ms. Hobbs made a point of criticizing Ms. Lake's anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance as ''extreme and out of touch.'' Ms. Lake has called the 1864 ban ''a great law'' and has said she would support further anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures as governor.\par \par \uc2 New polls of the governor's race -- a virtual dead heat -- suggest that those laws are out of step with an electorate that is getting younger and increasingly Latino and pulling a traditionally conservative state closer to the political center.\par \par \uc2 On her website, Ms. Lake pledges to support all forms of birth control, as well as state government programs to help pregnant mothers seek alternatives to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as adoption, and provide resources for parental support and guidance. She also says fathers must be ''held accountable.''\par \par \uc2 Some 90 percent of Arizona voters said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should always be legal, or should be legal in some circumstances, according to a survey conducted in early September by the Phoenix-based firm OH Predictive Insights. And 45 percent said that a candidate's stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  had a strong impact on their vote.\par \par \uc2 ''It's just scary,'' said Andrea Luna Cervantes, a \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive-rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  activist in Phoenix. ''Because you're a woman, because you're a person who can give birth, your rights can be just stripped.''\par \par \uc2 Ms. Cervantes said she got involved in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights activism after seeing people she knew face pregnancies with few resources or options other than carrying them to term. She said she planned to vote for Ms. Hobbs, but some family members back in Yuma were unconvinced.\par \par \uc2 The ban struck a chord with some Indigenous voters, who make up 5 percent of the state's population. Anjeanette Laban, a member of the Hopi Tribe, said \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  care was already dangerously scarce and distant. She saw the end of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in Arizona as another colonial oppression. She said that she knew little about the candidates running, but that the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue would determine her vote.\par \par \uc2 ''They're still trying to dictate what we can do, how they can limit us,'' she said.\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, Ms. Hobbs has been leaning into the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in email blasts to supporters, and the Arizona Democratic Party has released a new television ad slamming Ms. Lake for saying she did not believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal.\par \par \uc2 ''Since Roe v. Wade was overturned, Arizona has reverted back to a 100-year-old law that criminalizes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and Kari Lake -- she supports that,'' Chris Nanos, the Pima County sheriff, says in the ad.\par \par \uc2 After the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban ruling, Ms. Lake called Ms. Hobbs ''radical'' on the issue during an interview on Fox News. On Monday, she emailed supporters keeping up her critique of Ms. Hobbs on immigration. The subject line was ''Open Borders Katie.''\par \par \uc2 Katie Hobbs has spoken about her miscarriage and her need for a surgical procedure now being denied to women in some states.; Supporters of Kari Lake, Ms. Hobbs's Republican opponent, who has emphasized border security and election conspiracy theories. (PHOTOGRAPHS BY REBECCA NOBLE FOR THE NEW YORK TIMES); Supporters of \uc2  rights outside the Arizona Senate in June after the Supreme Court overturned the Roe v. Wade decision. (PHOTOGRAPH BY JOEL ANGEL JUAREZ/USA TODAY NETWORK, VIA REUTERS) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020220930ei9u00034\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
