\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 G.O.P. Unable To Find Unity Over  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Lisa Lerer and Elizabeth Dias \par \uc2 1,922 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 September 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A new proposal was intended to align Republicans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy before the midterm elections. It only exposed divisions.\par \par \uc2 For weeks, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists and their Republican allies have been quietly seeking to rally their party around a single platform on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , hoping to settle divisions and blunt political damage from an issue with growing potency in the midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 But when Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  came ahead on Tuesday with a proposed 15-week national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban intended to unite his party, the result was only more division.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Graham's Senate allies swiftly distanced themselves from the plan, reflecting a lack of consensus in the party, as well as deep resistance to being drawn into any debates over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  while economic issues hold more sway with swing voters.\par \par \uc2 The rapid rejection of Mr. Graham's gambit was the latest misfire in the party's struggle to unite behind a clear strategy on an issue that has reshaped campaigns across the country. Despite decades of Republican efforts to overturn Roe v. Wade, when the Supreme Court ultimately took that step in June, the G.O.P. was caught flat-footed, with no unified national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy ready to put into place.\par \par \uc2 While Democrats have been energized in the months since, vowing to fight for access and firing up their voters in the process, Republicans have offered a wide range of proposals and battled in state legislatures to enact them.\par \par \uc2 ''The Republican response has been disastrous,'' said Marjorie Dannenfelser, the president of Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America, who pushed for Mr. Graham's bill. But now, she said, ''They are finding their voice.''\par \par \uc2 Ms. Dannenfelser is now urging Senate candidates to endorse Mr. Graham's federal ban, which includes exceptions for rape, incest and the life or physical health of the mother. While the policy is more restrictive than previous Senate proposals, it falls well short of the six-week national ban some social conservatives have wanted. A 15-week limit could allow the vast majority of abortions to continue. (In 2019, 93 percent of abortions happened before 13 weeks of pregnancy, according to the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 .)\par \par \uc2 Some Republicans in the Senate greeted the idea dismissively. Senator \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , Republican of Kentucky and the minority leader, who has previously said that his party was unlikely to pursue an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, told reporters on Tuesday that he thought the issue should be left up to the states and that most members of his conference agreed.\par \par \uc2 When pressed on the details of Mr. Graham's bill, Mr. McConnell sought to distance himself, saying, ''You'll have to ask him about it.''\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2  of Texas told CNN that he preferred to ''have each state handle those issues.'' Senator Ron Johnson of Wisconsin demurred, and Senator \uc2 Thom Tillis\uc2  of North Carolina told the network that he wanted to focus on inflation.\par \par \uc2 There were no signs of G.O.P. division later Tuesday night at a gala hosted by Ms. Dannenfelser's group. Several senators toasted the demise of Roe. In his remarks, Mr. Graham promised to ''rally the Republican Party'' to ''protect the unborn.''\par \par \uc2 Since the court decision in June, candidates, activists and elected officials have championed a range of positions, from near-total bans and fetal personhood to restrictions as late as 20 weeks. At the same time, they have been battered by headlines highlighting the medical crises of pregnant women and girls, including stories of child rape and severe fetal abnormalities.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, West Virginia legislators passed new legislation banning nearly all abortions, but only after weeks of debate. An effort to advance hard-line restrictions has stalled in Republican-dominated South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Voters in Kansas overwhelmingly rejected an attempt to remove the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the State Constitution, and Democrats who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights have outperformed expectations in recent special elections. An earlier push from some anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists to introduce Senate legislation banning the procedure at around six weeks failed to gain traction.\par \par \uc2 The pushback prompted some Republican candidates to distance themselves from the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue, scrubbing their websites of their previous, hard-line positions. Others published op-eds and released ads reversing their previous stances. Many stopped mentioning the issue on the campaign trail, keeping the focus on inflation, gas prices and public safety that they believed could help them win over swing voters.\par \par \uc2 The backpedaling has worried some social conservatives, who fear that Republicans are not only ceding what they believe is a winning political issue but could be jeopardizing the push for further restrictions.\par \par \uc2 ''There's no doubt that there are a lot of G.O.P. consultants encouraging candidates to not talk about the issue,'' said Marc Short, who served as chief of staff to former Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , one of the country's highest-profile allies of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement. ''It is the wrong approach.''\par \par \uc2 Polls consistently show that a significant national majority back a federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Yet just as many Americans say they support banning most abortions in the second trimester, after about 12 weeks. Until this summer, the Roe v. Wade decision barred states from restricting access before about 23 weeks.\par \par \uc2 Some anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups are urging Republicans to try to use \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to their advantage. The Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America Candidate Fund has privately circulated new talking points to Senate candidates who oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , advising them to use a 15-week restriction to contrast themselves with Democrats.\par \par \uc2 The memo argued that the position would allow ''pro-life states to enact more aggressive limits,'' while also setting a ''baseline'' in Democratic-controlled states like California, New York and Illinois. Officials in those states are moving to dramatically expand \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access to accommodate women traveling from states where the procedure is restricted.\par \par \uc2 In a separate letter to Congress on Monday, S.B.A. Pro-Life America and about 100 state anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups urged federal lawmakers to ''find consensus'' and pass a federal limit.\par \par \uc2 Some strategists argue that Republicans can flip the script by defining Democrats as the extremists who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until the last moment of pregnancy. Many Democrats have declined to support a specific time limit, arguing that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a right that should be protected by federal law and is a health care decision that should be between a woman and her doctor.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Mr. Graham called his proposal a ''late-term'' \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, a political term with no precise medical definition and that is frequently used by Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Representative \uc2 Tom Emmer\uc2  of Minnesota, the chairman of the National Republican Congressional Committee, has falsely suggested that legislation codifying \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights would lead to forced abortions.\par \par \uc2 ''If they want to make that the central focus of their campaigns, they can do that. But they do it at their own risk,'' he said in an interview. The language carried echoes of the inflammatory rhetoric used by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups and President Trump, who in 2019 falsely claimed that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights allowed mothers and doctors to decide to ''execute'' a baby.\par \par \uc2 ''You have to fight the issue out,'' said Brad Todd, a Republican political consultant who is urging many of the party's Senate candidates to forcefully rebut Democratic attacks on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . ''And if you fight the issue out, you can win on it. But you can't just put your head in the sand and act like it's going to go away.''\par \par \uc2 Democrats counter that a Republican strategy can't erase decades of G.O.P. messaging that has cast \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as murder and that has argued that life begins at conception. Already, Democrats have spent millions on ads attacking their opponents for supporting national bans with no exceptions for rape and incest.\par \par \uc2 In a meeting with civil rights and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates on Monday, Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said the administration plans to increase its focus on the issue in the final weeks of the campaign, according to someone briefed on the event who asked not to be named, discussing private conversations. Within hours of Mr. Graham's introducing his proposal, Democrats across the country attempted to tie their opponents to the plan, saying that if elected, they would be ''automatic votes'' for a national ban in Congress.\par \par \uc2 ''We can look at all the differences between where they have been, things that have been said, but at the end of the day what is being proposed is a national ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and that stands in direct contrast with the will of the American people,'' said Laphonza Butler, the head of Emily's List, the largest funder of female Democratic candidates who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 For decades, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was an easy rallying call for the Republican Party. Politicians and party officials united with the active conservative base behind the broad, and somewhat vague, ''pro-life'' label.\par \par \uc2 But the court's ruling forced politicians to confront the far messier specifics of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. In a debate in Indiana over the summer, Republican lawmakers viciously fought over how far a total ban should go, wrestling under the national spotlight with questions about child rape, ectopic pregnancy and life-threatening medical complications from pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Some Republican political strategists are urging candidates to avoid talking about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as much as possible, saying that economic issues remain the number one concern for voters -- particularly swing voters.\par \par \uc2 ''My advice is, don't take the bait. If you are pro-life, say you are pro-life,'' said Kristin Davison, a G.O.P. strategist who worked on Gov. Glenn Youngkin's upset win in Virginia last year. ''Then, get back to the kitchen table.''\par \par \uc2 Some candidates have simply tried to avoid the issue. During an April primary debate, \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2 , the Republican nominee for governor in Pennsylvania, called legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ''a national catastrophe'' and vowed to push a proposal banning abortions after six weeks. But since winning his party's nomination in May, he has been largely silent on his \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  views.\par \par \uc2 In mid-April, Ohio Gov. \uc2 Mike DeWine\uc2 's campaign website trumpeted him as the ''the most pro-life governor in Ohio history,'' highlighting his 2019 signature on a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that became law after the Supreme Court decision. By midsummer, his website no longer mentioned the issue at all.\par \par \uc2 Republican candidates running in New Mexico and Washington have released ads attempting to clarify that they would oppose a national ban and protect access to contraception.\par \par \uc2 Despite the campaign rhetoric, many \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents still ultimately want the procedure to be banned at conception, with few if any exceptions.\par \par \uc2 A 15-week ban would be ''the beginning,'' said Kristan Hawkins, president of Students for Life of America and Students for Life Action, last week as she arrived at the Senate building. Ms. Hawkins said that she has been talking with congressional staff about introducing a federal ban on abortions after six weeks of pregnancy but called it a ''work in progress.''\par \par \uc2 ''Everyone here is focused on November,'' she said. ''We have our plans for January in place, but we've got to get to that point first.''\par \par \uc2 Annie Karni contributed reporting from Washington.\par \par \uc2 Annie Karni contributed reporting from Washington.\par \par \uc2 Senator Lindsey Graham, Republican of South Carolina, introduced a bill on Capitol Hill on Tuesday that would implement a national ban on abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy. (PHOTOGRAPH BY HAIYUN JIANG/THE NEW YORK TIMES) (A15) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020220914ei9e0004g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
