\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Rights Looming Large As a Start-Up Stirs Investors\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ephrat Livni \par \uc2 483 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 September 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 After the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade, Alinea, an investing app geared toward young adults, saw a new focus on companies that support \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In recent years, funds focused in investments that have a social impact have emerged to bet on start-ups advancing \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  and innovation. After the Supreme Court decision in June to overturn the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , individual investors turned their attention to \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 Almost immediately after the court's decision, Alinea, an investing app geared toward young adults, saw a new investment focus on companies that support \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Alinea's founders, Eve Halimi and Anam Lakhani.\par \par \uc2 ''When the news came out, one of the community members created a pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights playlist'' -- as in a basket of stocks -- ''with companies that were supporting the cause,'' Ms. Halimi told the DealBook newsletter. ''We saw a rush of activity.''\par \par \uc2 That first, spontaneous user-created playlist included companies that were taking a stand to support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, rather than those connected to women's health, echoing public demand for businesses to weigh in on the issue.\par \par \uc2 Later, users asked for an updated version of the playlist, and the founders adopted that same standard. It now includes about 50 firms -- Levi's, \uc2 Apple\uc2 , \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and \uc2 Tesla\uc2  among them -- that have taken a stand against the overturning of Roe v. Wade or help pay for employees' access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services, or both.\par \par \uc2 Data from the platform shows \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  looming large in investment decisions. But location and gender matter. One month after the decision, Alinea had about 10,000 female users. Of those:\par \par \uc2 About 11 percent are in Texas, where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access was threatened, and slightly more than half are now investing in companies that support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 About 25 percent are in New York City, where \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  remain robust, and only about 40 percent of them are investing in companies that support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 More than 30 percent of new app users now cite the change in \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a reason for their interest in both investing and financial independence.\par \par \uc2 No male users have invested in playlists that are made up of companies supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the corporate level are the newest frontier for the environmental, social and governance investing framework, according to Confluence Philanthropy, a network of investment managers, shareholder activists and others that convened a panel discussion on the matter in June. Expect a flurry of proxy proposals as activists plan to push deeper into the corporate arena. Previous efforts have failed, but E.S.G. experts are certainly telling companies to start preparing.\par \par \uc2 Eve Halimi, left, and Anam Lakhani are the founders of Alinea, an investing app geared toward young adults. (PHOTOGRAPH BY Alinea FOR THE NEW YORK TIMES) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020220902ei9200034\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
