\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Newsom Urges Hollywood To Back Up Liberal Values\b0\par\par\uc2 By Shawn Hubler \par \uc2 1,130 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 August 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 16\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The California governor says film companies should ''walk the walk'' on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and L.G.B.T.Q. protections by leaving states such as Georgia and Oklahoma.\par \par \uc2 SACRAMENTO -- Widening his attack on Republican states for their positions on guns, civil rights and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Gov. \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  of California on Wednesday called on Hollywood to ''walk the walk'' on liberal values by bringing back their film and television productions from states such as Georgia and Oklahoma.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Newsom issued the challenge through an ad in Variety that asked the state's left-leaning creative community to ''take stock of your values -- and those of your employees -- when doing business in those states.''\par \par \uc2 The Democratic governor on Wednesday simultaneously endorsed a legislative proposal that would provide a $1.65 billion, five-year extension of California's film and television production tax credit program.\par \par \uc2 It marked the second time in recent weeks that Mr. Newsom has used California legislation as a cudgel to rip Republican leaders elsewhere. Last month, he signed a bill allowing residents to sue makers of illegal guns and took the opportunity to rebuke Gov. Greg Abbott of Texas for previously enabling its residents to sue \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Newsom's statements on Wednesday underscored the pressure that intensifying culture wars have placed on U.S. corporations, particularly in states where the Supreme Court's reversal of Roe v. Wade has severely constrained \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  for women.\par \par \uc2 Some of the country's biggest businesses, including the \uc2 Walt Disney Company\uc2 , \uc2 Netflix\uc2  and \uc2 Comcast\uc2 , which owns \uc2 NBCUniversal\uc2 , have announced programs to help employees who need \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access but cannot obtain it in their home states. Hundreds of entertainment figures also have denounced policies in Republican-led states that have weakened safeguards for L.G.B.T.Q. people. Last week, some 400 television creators and showrunners publicly demanded that production companies protect pregnant employees in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is outlawed.\par \par \uc2 But entertainment companies have not yet announced major plans to cancel expansions or relocate offices. ''Tulsa King,'' Taylor Sheridan's upcoming crime drama starring Sylvester Stallone, has been filming this summer for Paramount+ in Oklahoma.\par \par \uc2 In Georgia on Monday, Gov. \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  announced that film and television productions generated $4.4 billion in the state this fiscal year, a new record. ''Spider-Man: No Way Home'' was filmed in the state, the governor noted, as was the fourth season of ''Stranger Things.''\par \par \uc2 ''I was happy to name \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  Oklahoma's Economic Developer of the Year Award in 2021 and I'm glad to see he's making a run for two years in a row,'' Gov. \uc2 Kevin Stitt\uc2  of Oklahoma joked in a statement on Wednesday. Mr. Stitt took a similar jab at the California governor last year in reference to the state's pandemic shutdowns, which Mr. Stitt said drove business to his state.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Motion Picture Association\uc2 , the trade group representing major film studios and \uc2 Netflix\uc2 , declined to comment on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Moving a production can be exceptionally costly and logistically complex, and some of the entertainment industry's biggest companies are deeply invested in states with conservative leaders. \uc2 Disney\uc2 , for example, has maintained extensive operations in Florida despite a bitter and expensive standoff between its employees and the state.\par \par \uc2 After \uc2 Disney\uc2  -- pressured by its employees -- opposed a Florida ban on L.G.B.T.Q.-related instruction, state legislators and Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  stripped the company of the special authority it had over the swaths of land where Disney World and other company properties are located. \uc2 Disney\uc2 , meanwhile, has delayed a planned relocation of some 2,000 high-profile jobs from California to Florida.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Newsom has been in the thick of that power struggle for months, trolling Mr. DeSantis on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  and inviting \uc2 Disney\uc2  to rethink its Florida investments. The Variety ad was the latest in a series of initiatives by Mr. Newsom to take his defense of ''California values'' onto a national stage.\par \par \uc2 A $105,000 spot that ran in Florida last month -- attacking Mr. DeSantis and inviting Florida businesses to come to California -- was the opening salvo in a national effort by Mr. Newsom that has included newspaper ads in Texas attacking Mr. Abbott on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions and a highly publicized trip to Washington, D.C., to discuss, among other things, gun legislation.\par \par \uc2 In widening his attacks to include Oklahoma and Georgia, Mr. Newsom targeted not only two of California's most aggressive rivals for film, television and other content production but two of the nation's most conservative states on social issues.\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma, which aggressively ramped up film production incentives during the pandemic, has banned nearly all abortions since the Roe v. Wade reversal. And Georgia, which has one of the nation's most generous packages of film production incentives, has granted fetuses full legal recognition. This week, a Georgia tax agency found that pregnant women could take a $3,000 personal tax exemption for any fetus with a detectable heartbeat.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Newsom noted that California's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are among the most secure in the nation. The state has also enacted some of the nation's toughest laws on gun safety and civil liberties for L.G.B.T.Q. people.\par \par \uc2 California's film tax credit -- which the state created in 2009 after productions began decamping for Canada -- has been of debatable value, even with an expansion and overhaul in 2014. The incentive allows filmmakers to recoup as much as 25 percent of their spending -- up to the first $100 million -- on crew salaries and other costs, excluding star salaries. But other states, including Georgia, offer more significant rebates.\par \par \uc2 Critics complain that the tax credit encourages bidding wars and rarely keeps productions in the state over the long term. A 2019 analysis by the state's nonpartisan Legislative Analyst's Office found that one-third of the projects that received the subsidies probably would have been made in California regardless.\par \par \uc2 ''While the credit probably caused some film and television projects to be made here, many other similar projects also were made here without receiving any financial incentive,'' the report said.\par \par \uc2 But Newsom on Wednesday touted another study, conducted this year for the \uc2 Motion Picture Association\uc2  by the Los Angeles County Economic Development Corp., that concluded that California's program had helped create more than 110,000 jobs and tens of billions of dollars in economic output. In recent years, the tax credit has also helped bring shows such as ''American Horror Story,'' ''Veep'' and ''Lucifer'' back from other states and countries to California.\par \par \uc2 Gov. Gavin Newsom of California speaking at a news conference in Sacramento in June. (PHOTOGRAPH BY Rich Pedroncelli/Associated Press FOR THE NEW YORK TIMES) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020220804ei8400048\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
